# Example environment file.
#
# This file documents ONLY the EZcount invoicing integration. Other variables
# (DB, SECRET, PORT, HYP_*, storage, SMS, ...) are supplied by the deploy
# environment and are intentionally not listed here.
#
# Copy the values you need into .env (local, git-ignored) or into the
# container/host environment (production). Never commit real credentials.
#
# .env is loaded by server/boot.js via process.loadEnvFile() when the file
# exists; containers normally receive these as real environment variables.

# ---- Credentials --------------------------------------------------------
# Normally stored in the encrypted `ezcount` Setting, scoped per domain:
#   node server/scripts/runSeedEzcountSetting.js --enabled true --api-key <key> --developer-email <email>
#
# The variables below are FALLBACKS: if the Setting has a value, the Setting
# wins. Leave them empty when the Setting is seeded -- otherwise a stale stored
# key silently takes precedence over the env one. The seed script also reads
# them, so an env-only setup works for a demo.
# EZCOUNT_API_KEY=
# EZCOUNT_DEVELOPER_EMAIL=

# Distributor accounts only: EZcount rejects the request without it. Ordinary
# accounts must leave it unset -- it is omitted from the body when empty.
# It must be the DISTRIBUTOR's key, not this account's own key: sending your own
# key fails with errNum 1 ("mandatory key for distributors users").
# EZCOUNT_CREATED_BY_API_KEY=

# Production: https://api.ezcount.co.il (default when unset)
# Demo:       https://demo.ezcount.co.il   (separate API key)
# EZCOUNT_BASE_URL=https://api.ezcount.co.il

# ---- Behaviour overrides ------------------------------------------------
# These OVERRIDE the stored Setting for EVERY domain, not just one. Prefer the
# per-domain Setting in production; use these for local runs and demo accounts.
#
# Parsing is strict: only the exact lowercase string `true` is truthy.
# `1`, `yes` and `True ` all evaluate to false. Use `false` to force off.
#
# EZCOUNT_ENABLED=false     # master switch; also required for config.ready
# EZCOUNT_AUTO_ISSUE=true   # issue the invoice automatically at J4 capture
# EZCOUNT_SHADOW_MODE=false # build and log the payload without calling EZcount

# ---- Env-only tuning (no Setting field) ---------------------------------
# EZCOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS=35000
# INVOICE_RETRY_CRON=*/10 * * * *
